# Data conversion between kibibyte and mebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kibibyte and mebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KiB to 0.0009MiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 0.0014MiB; backward, converting 1MiB to 1024KiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5MiB yields 1536.0KiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(forward_whole->to(MiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(forward_fractional->to(MiB))
backward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(backward_whole->to(KiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(backward_fractional->to(KiB))

<<< stdout
0.0009MiB
0.0014MiB
1024KiB
1536.0KiB

<<< stderr
